      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "https://docs.vrchat.com/docs/launch-options\n\nDocs say:\n\n--fps=X\tOverrides the FPS cap to X instead of the default. On Desktop, 90 is the default. In VR, the headset's reported maximum refresh rate is the default.\n\nI try both write/delete. VRChat rendering in 110FPS over.\n\nOfcourse this option is not working and Docs say lie.\n\nI check steamVR refleshRate, It's 60Hz.\n\nActually, I don't know what is \"the headset's reported maximum refresh rate\" but I think this is it. Up until now, VRChat refleshRate has always been 60FPS.\n\nHas the default changed?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
